# Dependency directories
node_modules/
# Why: Dependencies can be reinstalled via package.json/package-lock.json. Committing them wastes massive amounts of space.

# Next.js build output
.next/
out/
# Why: These are auto-generated build files. They should be generated locally or by a CI/CD server, not tracked in source control.

# Environment variables
.env
.env*.local
# Why: These files contain sensitive secrets, API keys, and database passwords. They must NEVER be committed.

# SQLite Databases
*.db
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
# Why: Local databases contain raw development data and change constantly. They cause massive merge conflicts and shouldn't be tracked.

# Local Uploads/Assets
/data/*
!/data/.gitkeep
/data/photos/*
!/data/photos/.gitkeep
# Why: Ignores actual uploaded photos or files while keeping the folder structure intact via .gitkeep.

# OS generated files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
# Why: System-specific metadata files that clutter the repository.

# Editor directories and files
.idea/
.vscode/
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
# Why: Personal IDE configurations shouldn't be forced on others (or your future self on a different machine).

# Private notes
project_notes_PRIVATE.md
# Why: Keeps your sensitive planning documents out of the repository.